ter you're  literally painting the movie  yeah you can uh you can affect it a lot  in the grade i mean hopefully at that  point you've got a pretty good sense  of what it is you're going for even if  it's a rough version in the avid  um but i like to do it with claudio you  know next to me um since you know he's  the cinematographer and we we shot it  together um  and yeah it's fun it's really for me  it's a fun part of the process if you  could ask imax to design a new camera or  cameras to help you as a filmmaker um  when you're filming a movie what would  you what would that request be smaller  is always better  um you know especially for a movie like  this from the movie i'm prepping now you  know which is dealing with uh  cars you know very fast cars on a race  track um trying to get cameras in places  um interesting places give the audience  perspectives um they've never had before  smaller lighter  is always a good thing is the 6k chip  that's in the venice camera like you  don't really do you need a chip that's  better quality or is it literally just  about shrinking the camera with the  current chip that you're using  i think the quality is is there i mean  the the projection format now is 4k so  we're already have more resolution  uh than we need which is good um in case  you want to you know  blow into something a little bit you  want to have that extra resolution but  yeah it's it's just about getting the  you know if you can get it down to just  a sensor and a lens  um that would be ideal because you could  put it anywhere as you know i i love the  imax format and and think it's the way  to watch movies um do you see yourself  in the future with like the movie you're  working on now and things down the road  do you think imax will always be a  component that you would like to you  know collaborate with absolutely you  know the great thing about an imax  theater is when you walk into it you  know the picture is going to be bright  enough  the sound is no